  txLevelRange: {fileID: 816591786473953547}
  txDescription: {fileID: 6158402248592766329}
  descriptions:
  - "An outdoor trip is a group activity that usually takes place in parks, beaches,
    forests, or nature reserves. It\u2019s a chance for people to step away from
    their daily surroundings, enjoy the beauty of nature, relax, and recharge their
    energy. More than just fun, outdoor trips also encourage teamwork, build awareness
    of protecting the environment, and bring people closer together. That\u2019s
    why schools, companies, and families often choose excursions as a meaningful
    way to combine learning and leisure."
  - Swimming in the sea is a familiar and enjoyable recreational activity, often
    taking place at beaches during the summer. Immersing in the cool, clear water
    not only helps people beat the heat but also improves health and enhances physical
    flexibility. The waves, sea breeze, and warm sunlight bring a sense of relaxation
    and refresh the spirit. Beyond relaxation and exercise, swimming in the sea is
    also associated with fun group experiences, creating memorable moments during
    trips with family and friends.
  - Taking a walk is a simple activity, yet it brings many benefits for both health
    and the mind. Usually done in parks, along quiet streets, or by the lakeside,
    walking helps the body move gently, improves blood circulation, and reduces stress
    after long hours of work. It is also a chance to breathe fresh air, enjoy the
    surrounding scenery, and find a sense of peace in everyday life. Because it is
    convenient and easy to do, walking has become a healthy habit suitable for people
    of all ages.
  - Desert exploration is an adventurous form of tourism that offers people the chance
    to discover vast, arid, and mysterious landscapes. Amid endless golden sands,
    travelers can experience camel riding, drive off-road vehicles across towering
    dunes, or admire the majestic beauty of desert sunsets. Beyond recreation, this
    activity also provides insights into the harsh yet culturally rich life of local
    inhabitants. The blend of challenge, discovery, and culture has made desert exploration
    an appealing journey for many tourists around the world.
  - 'Kite flying is a traditional pastime not only in Vietnam but also in many parts
    of the world. In countries such as Japan, Korea, India, and Thailand, kite flying
    has become a cultural tradition closely associated with festivals. Each place
    has its own styles, colors, and meanings: carp-shaped kites in Japan symbolize
    strength and perseverance, dragon kites in China represent the aspiration to
    rise high, while in India, grand kite festivals attract thousands of participants
    every year. Today, kite flying is not only a graceful form of entertainment but
    also a community activity that celebrates creativity and brings joy to people
    of all ages across the globe.'
  btSetBG: {fileID: 6837225874667799908}
