  m_text: 'Kite flying is a traditional pastime not only in Vietnam but also in many
    parts of the world. In countries such as Japan, Korea, India, and Thailand, kite
    flying has become a cultural tradition closely associated with festivals. Each
    place has its own styles, colors, and meanings: carp-shaped kites in Japan symbolize
    strength and perseverance, dragon kites in China represent the aspiration to
    rise high, while in India, grand kite festivals attract thousands of participants
    every year. Today, kite flying is not only a graceful form of entertainment but
    also a community activity that celebrates creativity and brings joy to people
    of all ages across the globe.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e1c44b8c4cd0f4b4ab0227fc7a484d8d, type: 2}
